---
layout: layouts/base.njk
description: Local ham radio events, nets, repeaters and special event stations around Middletown, Ohio, plus a friendly guide to getting started in amateur radio.
permalink: /
---
{% from "partials/macros.njk" import eventItem %}

<section class="hero">
  <div class="wrap hero__inner">
    <p class="eyebrow">Amateur radio · {{ site.communities | join(" · ") }}</p>
    <h1>Hi, I'm <span class="mono callsign">{{ site.callsign }}</span>.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      I'm a licensed ham radio operator in Middletown, Ohio. This is my corner of the
      internet for local radio happenings: what's on the calendar, where the nets and
      meetups are, and how to get started if you're curious.
    </p>
    <p class="hero__actions">
      <a class="button" href="/events/">See upcoming events</a>
      <a class="button button--ghost" href="/get-started/">New to ham radio? Start here</a>
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="dial-rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
</section>

<section class="wrap section" aria-labelledby="next-h">
  <div class="section__head">
    <h2 id="next-h">Coming up</h2>
    <a href="/events/">All events →</a>
  </div>
  {%- set next = cal.upcoming | take(5) %}
  <ol class="event-list" data-upcoming-list>
    {%- for ev in next %}
    {{ eventItem(ev) }}
    {%- endfor %}
  </ol>
  <p class="empty" data-empty{% if next.length %} hidden{% endif %}>
    Nothing is on the calendar right now. Check back soon, or <a href="/local-info/">see the regular nets and meetings</a>.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="wrap section teaser" aria-labelledby="what-h">
  <h2 id="what-h">What is ham radio?</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Ham radio</strong> (also called <strong>amateur radio</strong>) is a hobby and public service
    where licensed people use radio to talk with each other, near and far, without
    needing the internet or a cell tower. Hams talk across town through
    <strong>repeaters</strong> (radio relay stations on tall towers), reach other
    countries on shortwave, bounce signals off the moon, and keep communications
    running when storms knock out everything else.
  </p>
  <p>
    Anyone can get a license: you study, pass a multiple-choice exam, and
    you're on the air. It's a hobby for tinkerers, talkers, and people who like to help.
  </p>
  <p><a class="button" href="/get-started/">How to get licensed</a></p>
</section>
